  "exit_criteria": [
    "Name the main components of wheat flour (gliadin, glutenin, starch, damaged starch, arabinoxylans, lipids, enzymes) and give the role of each in dough",
    "Explain how hydration, kneading and rest build a gluten network through disulfide and hydrogen bonding, and why gliadin and glutenin contribute different properties",
    "Predict how salt, time and temperature change dough strength and fermentation, and justify each prediction mechanistically",
    "Describe yeast and lactic/acetic acid bacteria metabolism, and explain where bread's rise, flavor and sourness come from",
    "Explain viscoelasticity, elasticity vs. extensibility and gas retention conceptually, and link them to shaping and proofing decisions",
    "Walk through the oven sequence (oven spring, starch gelatinization, protein setting, Maillard browning vs. caramelization, the role of steam)",
    "Explain staling as starch retrogradation and choose the right storage method",
    "Contrast enriched, rye and gluten-free doughs with lean wheat dough by asking what replaces or weakens the gluten network",
    "Calculate hydration, salt percentage and preferment percentage with baker's percentages",
    "Diagnose common bread defects (dense crumb, flying crust, pale crust, gummy interior, collapse) by tracing them to a cause in a specific stage"
